; =====================================================================
; updates.abnf
;
; VERBATIM.  RFC 9682's four figures that STATE the change to RFC 8610's
; grammar, copied unchanged and NOT authored by this project.  Each is
; reproduced with the source's own leading comment line, which is part
; of the displayed figure.
;
; Locator:  RFC 9682, "Updates to the Concise Data Definition Language
;           (CDDL) Grammar", C. Bormann, November 2024, Standards
;           Track, ISSN 2070-1721.  Updates: 8610.
;           <https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9682.txt>
;
; Source digest (sha256 of the full cached source text):
;   d35602e7f784e509a5984283ea8d998adfee23f086ad0d77bd22f98c6cdea89c
;
; These four figures are the normative deltas.  Every rule here also
; appears in cddl-updated.abnf, which is the collected result; this file
; exists because the deltas are what a reader holding RFC 8610 needs,
; and because three of the four figure captions name the RFC 8610
; appendix each one amends.  Captions, quoted:
;
;   Figure 2   "Update to String ABNF in Appendix B of [RFC8610]: Allow
;               Hex Escapes"                       (source lines 159-160)
;   Figure 4   "Update to ABNF in Appendix B of [RFC8610]: BCHAR,
;               SCHAR, and PCHAR"                  (source lines 200-201)
;   Figure 8   "Update to Top-Level ABNF in Appendices B and C of
;               RFC 8610"                          (source line  301)
;   Figure 10  "Update to Tag and Simple Value ABNF in Appendices B
;               and C of RFC 8610"                 (source lines 326-327)
;
; NOTE THE SCOPE OF FIGURES 8 AND 10: both name "Appendices B and C of
; RFC 8610" -- that is, the collected ABNF *and* Appendix C's matching
; rules.  Figures 2 and 4 name Appendix B only.  Appendix A of the
; present document reproduces only the collected ABNF; it does not
; reproduce RFC 8610 Appendix C, so the Appendix C half of Figures 8 and
; 10 is stated in these captions and nowhere else in RFC 9682.
;
; THE CASE-SENSITIVITY NOTE belongs with Figure 2 and is reproduced here
; because Appendix A does not carry it.  Source lines 162-165, AS AN EXACT
; LINE RUN with the RFC's own "      |" aside prefix intact -- including
; the two trailing spaces the source puts after the "|" on each line.
; The prefix is NOT removed: normalising whitespace across an aside
; interleaves "|" into the text, so no sentence spanning two of these
; lines is a contiguous span of the document, and flowing one would be a
; silent repair.  Each line below is the source line with a leading ";"
; added so that this file stays valid ABNF.
;
;      |  Notes: In ABNF, strings such as "A", "B", etc., are case
;      |  insensitive, as is intended here.  The rules above could have
;      |  also used %s"b", etc., instead of %x62, but didn't, in order to
;      |  maximize compatibility with ABNF tools.
;
; The RFC's three-column left margin is preserved.  Not tool-consumable;
; see cddl-updated-dedented.derived.abnf.
; =====================================================================

; ---- BEGIN VERBATIM FIGURE-2 (SESC and the hexchar family) (source lines 145-157, sha256 549df9b2dc07c7e567accf0fdaf877bee5733bce0c55e6c839f0b581132d7d2a) ----
   ; new rules collectively defining SESC:
   SESC = "\" ( %x22 / "/" / "\" /                 ; \" \/ \\
                %x62 / %x66 / %x6E / %x72 / %x74 / ; \b \f \n \r \t
                (%x75 hexchar) )                   ; \uXXXX
   hexchar = "{" (1*"0" [ hexscalar ] / hexscalar) "}" /
             non-surrogate / (high-surrogate "\" %x75 low-surrogate)
   non-surrogate = ((DIGIT / "A"/"B"/"C" / "E"/"F") 3HEXDIG) /
                   ("D" %x30-37 2HEXDIG )
   high-surrogate = "D" ("8"/"9"/"A"/"B") 2HEXDIG
   low-surrogate = "D" ("C"/"D"/"E"/"F") 2HEXDIG
   hexscalar = "10" 4HEXDIG / HEXDIG1 4HEXDIG
             / non-surrogate / 1*3HEXDIG
   HEXDIG1 = DIGIT1 / "A" / "B" / "C" / "D" / "E" / "F"
; ---- END VERBATIM FIGURE-2 (SESC and the hexchar family) ----

; ---- BEGIN VERBATIM FIGURE-4 (SCHAR, BCHAR, PCHAR, NONASCII) (source lines 194-198, sha256 aa92663154f6e44e8a941d5749ab246fd797f76e735d3840b380490acb2b4908) ----
   ; new rules for SCHAR, BCHAR, and PCHAR:
   SCHAR = %x20-21 / %x23-5B / %x5D-7E / NONASCII / SESC
   BCHAR = %x20-26 / %x28-5B / %x5D-7E / NONASCII / SESC / "\'" / CRLF
   PCHAR = %x20-7E / NONASCII
   NONASCII = %xA0-D7FF / %xE000-10FFFD
; ---- END VERBATIM FIGURE-4 (SCHAR, BCHAR, PCHAR, NONASCII) ----

; ---- BEGIN VERBATIM FIGURE-8 (top-level rule cddl) (source lines 298-299, sha256 701610c1cbcee1ccf5b0fac48fd2a7cefee3f67c6a58eda021ff9dbb0647b683) ----
   ; new top-level rule:
   cddl = S *(rule S)
; ---- END VERBATIM FIGURE-8 (top-level rule cddl) ----

; ---- BEGIN VERBATIM FIGURE-10 (type2 tag/simple-value alternatives, head-number) (source lines 321-324, sha256 70949dbb4dfb014648ef16024199a8353c7caf9d2e962b3de6c4a34b1ff3c512) ----
   ; new rules collectively defining the tagged case:
   type2 =/ "#" "6" ["." head-number] "(" S type S ")"
          / "#" "7" ["." head-number]
   head-number = uint / ("<" type ">")
; ---- END VERBATIM FIGURE-10 (type2 tag/simple-value alternatives, head-number) ----
